{"name":"Knight’s Armour","hex":"#5c5d5d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"knight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young servant or follower; a trained military attendant in service of a lord.","A minor nobleman with an honourable military rank who had served as a page and squire."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To confer knighthood upon.","To promote (a pawn) to a knight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knight"},{"term":"armour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["British standard spelling of armor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["British standard spelling of armor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/armour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plate armour","blocks":[{"text":"Plate armour is a historical type of personal body armour made from bronze, iron, or steel plates, culminating in suits of armour which entirely or mostly encased the wearer. Full plate steel armour developed in Europe during the Late Middle Ages, especially in the context of the Hundred Years' War, from the coat of plates worn over mail suits during the 14th century, a century famous for transitional armour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Lossy-page1-2122px-H%C3%A4strustning_-_Livrustkammaren_-_72697_aaa.jpg/330px-Lossy-page1-2122px-H%C3%A4strustning_-_Livrustkammaren_-_72697_aaa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plate_armour","wikidata":"Q3391846"},{"title":"Armour","blocks":[{"text":"Armour or armor is a covering used to protect an object, individual, or vehicle from physical injury or damage, especially direct contact weapons or projectiles during combat, or from a potentially dangerous environment or activity. Personal armour is used to protect soldiers and war animals. Vehicle armour is used on warships, armoured fighting vehicles, and some combat aircraft, mostly ground attack aircraft."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Xixia_Chainmail_Armor_%2841985701161%29.jpg/330px-Xixia_Chainmail_Armor_%2841985701161%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armour","wikidata":"Q11886611"},{"title":"Knight","blocks":[{"text":"A knight is a person granted an honorary title of a knighthood by a head of state or representative for service to the monarch, the church, or the country, especially in a military capacity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg/330px-Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight","wikidata":"Q102083"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Rustning%2C_Gustav_Vasa_-_Livrustkammaren_-_32921.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Rustning%2C_Gustav_Vasa_-_Livrustkammaren_-_32921.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Rustning%2C_Gustav_Vasa_-_Livrustkammaren_-_32921.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Rustning%2C_Gustav_Vasa_-_Livrustkammaren_-_32921.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Rustning%2C_Gustav_Vasa_-_Livrustkammaren_-_32921.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Rustning%2C_Gustav_Vasa_-_Livrustkammaren_-_32921.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Armour for Gustav I of Sweden by Kunz Lochner, c. 1540 (Livrustkammaren).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARustning%2C_Gustav_Vasa_-_Livrustkammaren_-_32921.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Bronze_cuirass_BM_GR1873.8-20.223.jpg/500px-Bronze_cuirass_BM_GR1873.8-20.223.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=